t).  The case \nagainst overruling Chevron is at least as strong. In partic-', 'citation_text': '588 U. S., at 586'}], 'metadata': {'reporter': None, 'volume': None, 'page': None, 'year': None, 'court': None}}, {'text': '588 U. S., at 587', 'name': 'Unknown Case', 'valid': None, 'contexts': [{'text': 'ions” of statutes and threatening the interests of many parties who have relied on them for years.  588 U. S., at 587 (opinion of the Court). \nAdherence to precedent is “a foundation stone of the rule\nof law.” Michiga', 'citation_text': '588 U. S., at 587'}, {'text': 'ions” of statutes and threatening the interests of many parties who have relied on them for years.  588 U. S., at 587 (opinion of the Court). \nAdherence to precedent is “a foundation stone of the rule\nof law.” Michiga', 'citation_text': '588 U. S., at 587'}, {'text': 'ions” of statutes and threatening the interests of many parties who have relied on them for years.  588 U. S., at 587 (opinion of the Court). \nAdherence to precedent is “a foundation stone of the rule\nof law.” Michiga', 'citation_text': '588 U. S., at 587'}, {'text': 'ions” of statutes and threatening the interests of many parties who have relied on them for years.  588 U. S., at 587 (opinion of the Court). \nAdherence to precedent is “a foundation stone of the rule\nof law.” Michiga', 'citation_text': '588 U. S., at 587'}], 'metadata': {'reporter': None, 'volume': None, 'page': None, 'year': None, 'court': None}}, {'text': '501 U. S., at 827', 'name': 'Unknown Case', 'valid': None, 'contexts': [{'text': 's  “promotes the even-\nhanded, predictable, and consistent development of legalprinciples.” Payne , 501 U. S., at 827.  It enables people to\norder their lives in reliance on judicial decisions.  And it “contributes to', 'citation_text': '501 U. S., at 827'}], 'metadata': {'reporter': None, 'volume': None, 'page': None, 'year': None, 'court': None}}, {'text': '597 U. S., at 388', 'name': 'Unknown Case', 'valid': None, 'contexts': [{'